# Uptime Kuma monitors on {{ inventory_hostname }}

<!-- {{ ansible_managed }} -->

Uptime Kuma keeps its monitors in its own database and offers no supported configuration file
or API for them, so create each monitor below once by hand: open Uptime Kuma (published on
{{ __monitoring_uptime_kuma_publish.rsplit(':', 1)[0] }}, reached through its tunnel hostname),
choose "Add New Monitor" and copy the values. Add a notification (for example a Discord
webhook) under Settings, Notifications, and attach it to each monitor. Never put a password or
token into a monitor; Uptime Kuma stores them in clear text.

